# JS and CSS file size (project-authored code)

## Rule

- Each **project-authored** `.js` and `.css` file **must not exceed 300 lines**. Split before crossing that limit.
- For non-trivial modules, **aim for roughly 200–300 lines** so each file stays focused. **Shorter files are fine** for entry points (e.g. `main.js`), tiny utilities, or thin style layers when merging would be artificial.
- Prefer **clear names** and **one responsibility per file** over arbitrary splits.

## Exceptions

- **Third-party or generated snapshots** copied verbatim (e.g. a full theme stylesheet such as `src/styles/vcard.css` from an external template) may exceed the limit until intentionally refactored. When refactoring vendor CSS, split into logical partials and compose with `@import` (order matters for cascade).

## When editing

- Before adding a large block, check the file line count; extract helpers or partials first.
- After splitting, run the app (`npm run dev`) and a production build (`npm run build`) to verify bundles and styles.
